.TH VARDEFM 1 "2026-11-10" "vardefm 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vardefm \- open high-speed data modem for FM radios
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vardefm
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
VardeFM is an open-source, cross-platform high-speed data modem for FM radios.
It is a drop-in alternative to VARA FM for Winlink and similar apps (both
stations need VardeFM). Host programs talk to it over VARA's TCP
command/data interface (default ports 8300/8301).
.PP
Full user guide: /usr/share/doc/vardefm/README.md,
radio setup: /usr/share/doc/vardefm/RADIO.md,
protocol: /usr/share/doc/vardefm/PROTOCOL.md.
Upstream: https://github.com/notepid/vardeFM
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B modem
Run the modem on a real radio, with VARA-compatible TCP ports.
Example: vardefm modem \-\-audio\-in "USB" \-\-audio\-out "USB" \-\-ptt cm108
.TP
.B sim-pair
Two VardeFM stations in one process joined by a simulated FM link.
.TP
.B monitor
Show the receive level and decode any VardeFM bursts heard.
.TP
.B devices
List sound cards, CM108/CM119-type PTT devices and serial ports.
.TP
.B ptt-test
Key the transmitter briefly to check the PTT wiring.
.TP
.B tone
Transmit a test tone to set the transmit level (FM deviation).
.TP
.B bench
Measure whether this computer decodes fast enough for each mode and level.
.TP
.B sim, sweep, tx-wav, rx-wav, decode
Test, measurement and WAV tools (see --help output).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help (also: vardefm <command> \-\-help).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/99-vardefm-cm108.rules
udev rules letting group "audio" key CM108/CM119/AIOC PTT without root.
.SH EXAMPLES
vardefm devices
.br
vardefm ptt-test --ptt cm108
.br
vardefm monitor --audio-in "USB"
.br
vardefm modem --audio-in "USB" --audio-out "USB" --ptt cm108
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rigctld (1),
.BR pat (1)
